  Draft says the ceremony was on a Vijayadashami day specifically; article only says the event was Vijayadashami festival (acceptable), but the reel_script's 'விஜயதசமி நாளில்' is fine — however the caption and slides describe the children being seated on fathers' laps and writing 'அ' on rice, while the article says the purohit did this; slides_spec attributes the rice writing to the children generally, which is consistent with article wording.
  Slide 2 states 'பள்ளித் தலைவர் பெற்றோரை வரவேற்று வாழ்த்தினார்' — article says the school head welcomed parents and gave a greeting speech, which matches, but the slide omits that the purohit delivered the speech, which is mixed into the same list without clarity.
  reel_script and slides say 'புரோகிதர் உரையாற்றினார்' as a separate item while the article says the purohit spoke about education, knowledge and good values; the important content of his speech is missing from the reel_script.
  Reel_script says 'பள்ளி நிர்வாகத்தினரும் ஆசிரியர்களும் குழந்தைகளை வாழ்த்தினர்' but the article lists administrative head, treasurer, secretary, academic advisers, principals and teachers giving blessings; the draft's description is incomplete but not wrong.
  Caption and headline describe the event as 'மழலையருக்கு கல்வி தொடக்கம்' which matches the article's term for the event.
